1
00:00:01,333 --> 00:00:04,041
Part 1: What is mucositis?

2
00:00:04,708 --> 00:00:08,583
Radiation works mostly on rapidly dividing
cells.

3
00:00:08,583 --> 00:00:11,958
Your tumor is rapidly
dividing and growing,

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
and we want radiation to kill the tumor.

5
00:00:17,458 --> 00:00:18,500
However,

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,083
your mucosal membranes are also rapidly
dividing.

7
00:00:22,083 --> 00:00:25,500
As cells are secreting fluids
to line your mouth and throat.

8
00:00:26,291 --> 00:00:28,791
These cells are sensitive to radiation

9
00:00:28,791 --> 00:00:32,500
and can become inflamed
or irritated during radiation.

10
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,333
This is mucositis.

11
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:39,166
Mucositis, may first appear
 as red as tender tissue

12
00:00:39,166 --> 00:00:42,791
along your tongue,
back of your mouth, and throat.

13
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:45,958
If it worsens, you may notice

14
00:00:45,958 --> 00:00:49,833
some white spots or ulcers along
the tongue, cheek, or throat.

15
00:00:50,541 --> 00:00:54,250
They likely will be painful
and sensitive to touch.

16
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:59,125
Sometimes you can see them yourself by
shining light and looking into the mirror.

17
00:00:59,458 --> 00:01:04,208
Your doctor will also examine you weekly
during treatment to look for mucositis.
